SYNTHESIS
  In this bounded-base audit, every k=8..12 maximum occurs at
  b=k-1, r=1, core=consec_{k-1}, i.e. the one-stranger plateau Q(k-1).
  This supports the incoming KPS S19 decorrelation foundation.
  Remaining work is not this finite comparison; it is the explicit
  Weyl/decorrelation error and finite glue from bounded-gap rows.
  No LRC(14) proof is claimed.
